{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And when he saw that he could not prevail against him</b> — His angels are mighty ones of strength, doers of His word, and therefore the angel could not prevail against him to harm him, for he was not given permission except in what he did to him — to dislocate the hollow of his thigh. And they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 77:3): he touched all the righteous who were destined to come from him — this is the generation of the decree of destruction. And the meaning is that the entire event is an allusion to his generations: there would be a generation in the seed of Jacob over whom Esau would overpower them until he would nearly uproot their very essence, and this was one generation in the days of the Sages of the Mishnah, like the generation of Rabbi Yehuda ben Bava and his colleagues, as they said (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 2:7): Rabbi Chiya bar Abba said, if a man says to me, give your life for the sanctification of the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He, I give it, provided they kill me at once, but in the generation of the decree of destruction I cannot endure. And what would they do in the generation of the decree of destruction? They would bring iron grids and heat them in the fire and place them under their spines and scorch their souls from them. And there are other generations that did the like to us and worse than this, and all of it we bore and it passed over us, as he hinted: <i>and Jacob came whole</i>."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Reading כַּף יְרֵכוֹ (hollow of his thigh) and שֶׁחְיֵיהֶן (their spines) as printed; some editions read שִׁדְיֵיהֶן (their breasts). The lemma verse reference follows Ramban's citation of Genesis 32:26 (וַיַּרְא כִּי לֹא יָכֹל לוֹ)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:49.517957474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}